# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored.
#
# THEIR PROVIDER, NOT OURS. Use whichever provider you already hold a key for -- a kit that
# hardcodes one vendor is broken for most of the people who fork it. PROVIDER picks the adapter,
# MODEL picks the model behind it, and swapping either is this file plus one more run.
#
# ⚑ YOU DO NOT NEED A KEY TO SEE THIS KIT WORK, AND ON THIS ONE THE FREE HALF IS THE ARGUMENT.
# The corpus is generated from a fixed seed, and everything up to the model is pure code: cutting
# the stream into windows, collapsing 47 identical lines into one, detecting a service that has
# gone silent, and running the rule-and-threshold pager that most teams are actually using.
#
#     python3 tools/build_corpus.py     # the corpus, byte-identical every time
#     python3 -m evals.check_labels     # the labels, re-derived from the stream and checked
#     python3 -m evals.baseline         # a WORKING pager, scored over 49 settings, 0 calls, $0.00
#     python3 -m src.app                # the panel; drag the threshold, nothing is sent anywhere
#
# A key is needed only to ask the model about one window (one call per click) or to run the eval.
#
# ⚠︎ IF THIS KIT SITS INSIDE THE KITS REPO, IT ALREADY INHERITS THE ROOT .env AND THEREFORE A LIVE
# KEY. "I have not configured anything yet" is not the same as "nothing can spend". Check
# /api/status, or `python3 -m evals.run --dry-run`, before touching anything that calls out.

PROVIDER=openai-compatible
BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
API_KEY=
MODEL=

# No EMBED_MODEL: nothing is embedded. A window is judged from its own lines plus one computed fact
# about what is missing from them -- which is also why this kit's breaks_at_scale limit is about
# window volume and prompt size, not about a vector index.
